g/wiki/Hepatic_stellate_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000632 \"A cell that is found in the perisinusoidal space of the liver that is capable of multiple roles including storage of retinol, presentation of antigen to T cells (including CD1d-restricted NKT cells), and upon activation, production of extracellular matrix components that can contribute to liver fibrosis. This activated state has a myofibroblast-like phenotype, though it's not clear in the literature if this is terminally differentiated. This cell type comprises approximately 8-15% of total cells in the liver.\")\n9687:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000680 \"A non-terminally differentiated cell that is capable of developing into a muscle cell.\")\n10182:# Class: obo:CL_0000743 (hypertrophic chondrocyte)\n10184:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15951842\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000743 \"Chondrocyte that is terminally differentiated, produces type X collagen, is large in size, and often associated with the replacement of cartilage by bone (endochondral ossification).\")\n10186:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000743 \"hypertrophic chondrocyte\")\n10635:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19447676\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20081059\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20839338\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20951740\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plasma_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000786 \"A terminally differentiated, post-mitotic, antibody secreting cell of the B cell lineage with the phenotype CD138-positive, surface immunonoglobulin-negative, and MHC Class II-negative. Plasma cells are oval or round with extensive rough endoplasmic reticulum, a well-developed Golgi apparatus, and a round nucleus having a characteristic cartwheel heterochromatin pattern and are devoted to producing large amounts of immunoglobulin.\")\n13382:# Class: obo:CL_0001039 (terminally differentiated osteoblast)\n13384:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"VSAO:curator\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001039 \"Osteoblast that is terminally differentiated, located adjacent to acellular or cellular bone tissue within periosteum, and is capable of mineralizing the matrix.\")\n13386:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001039 \"terminally differentiated osteoblast\")\n13389:# Class: obo:CL_0001040 (non-terminally differentiated osteoblast)\n13391:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"VSAO:curator\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001040 \"Osteoblast that is non-terminally differentiated and located in cellular bone tissue or under the periosteum in acellular bone.\")\n13394:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001040 \"non-terminally differentiated osteoblast\")\n13645:# Class: obo:CL_0001062 (effector memory CD8-positive, alpha-beta T cell, terminally differentiated)\n13652:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001062 \"effector memory CD8-positive, alpha-beta T cell, terminally differentiated\")\n13835:# Class: obo:CL_0001087 (effector memory CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell, terminally differentiated)\n13844:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001087 \"effector memory CD4-positive, alpha-beta T cell, terminally differentiated\")\n19265:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MP:0008788\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002495 \"A fetal and neonatal heart cell that undergoes proliferation and is not yet terminally differentiated into a binucleate or a multinucleate cardiac myocyte.\")\n22355:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005001 \"A non-terminally differentiated cell that originates from the neural crest and differentiates into an iridophore.\")\n22363:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005002 \"A non-terminally differentiated cell that differentiates into a xanthophore.\")\n22370:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005003 \"A non-terminally differentiated cell that originates from the neural crest and differentiates into a leucophore.\")\n22377:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005004 \"A non-terminally differentiated cell that originates from the neural crest and differentiates into an erythrophore.\")\n22384:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005005 \"A non-terminally differentiated cell that originates from the neural crest and differentiates into a cyanophore.\")\n22689:# Class: obo:CL_0007012 (non-terminally differentiated odontoblast)\n22691:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PSPUB:0000170\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0007012 \"Odontoblast that non-terminally differentiated, located in the odontogenic papilla and dentine tissue, and transforms from a odontoblast cell.\")\n22692:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0007012 \"non-terminally differentiated odontoblast\")\n22696:# Class: obo:CL_0007013 (terminally differentiated odontoblast)\n22698:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000034\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0007013 \"Odontoblast that is terminally differentiated and derived from an odontogenic papilla and associated with dentine.\")\n22699:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0007013 \"terminally differentiated odontoblast\")\n25028:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0011115 \"Work is needed on GO 'cell differentiation' before it is clear whether the equivalent class definition 'native cell' that capable_of some 'cell differentiation' works. Also, may want to consider merging this with non-terminally differentiated cell.\")\n25601:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39759119\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020018 \"A fibrochondrocyte located in fibrocartilage that exhibits active proliferation capacity and is in S phase of the cell cycle. It functions as a progenitor cell positioned at the root of developmental trajectories alongside fibrochondrocyte progenitors (FCP), with the capacity to diverge toward one of two developmental fates: (1) fibrochondrocytes and prehypertrophic chondrocytes, or (2) regulatory chondrocytes and prehypertrophic chondrocytes. It is characterised by co-expression of COL1A1, the growth factors FGF7 and CTGF, and the cell-cycle genes STMN1, KIAA0101, and MCM3 in humans. During early progenitor differentiation, FGF7 and COL1A1 expression increases and then declines as the cell commits to terminal fates.\")\n26084:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28028137\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1000308 \"A stromal cell that is part of the outer adventitial layer of the ureter. This cell type is marked by expression of periostin (POSTN) in mice, and it is derived from Foxd1+ mesenchymal progenitors around embryonic day 12.5. The adventitial fibrocyte initiates differentiation earlier than smooth muscle cells and becomes terminally differentiated by E16.5-18.5 in mice, exhibiting low proliferative capacity in adulthood.\")\n31565:# Class: obo:CL_4030002 (effector memory CD45RA-positive, alpha-beta T cell, terminally differentiated)\n31572:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25104859\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030002 \"terminally differentiated effector memory CD45RA+ T cells\")\n31573:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/T_cell#Memory_T_cells\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030002 \"terminally differentiated effector memory cells re-expressing CD45RA\")\n31574:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030002 \"effector memory CD45RA-positive, alpha-beta T cell, terminally differentiated\")\n32089:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41385-022-00565-0\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030056 \"A urothelial cell that is terminally differentiated and part of the urothelial apical surface that forms the high-resistance barrier of urothelium. Umbrella cells have been described as the largest of urothelial cell types, highly polarized, and, in some species, multinucleated. In the relaxed state, these cells form a dome-shaped structure at the apical pole and can also cover multiple underlying intermediate cells, leading to the name umbrella cells. In contrast, these cells flatten when the bladder is filled.\")\n32810:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24079581\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28098391\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30969555\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34099859\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39451193\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033056 \"A terminally differentiated, specialized keratinocyte originating primarily from the nail matrix. During onychokeratinization, these cells undergo progressive flattening and produce high levels of hard, disulfide cross-linked keratins (Eckhart et al., 2024) that form the rigid, compact nail plate. Unlike epidermal keratinocytes, onychocytes are firmly integrated into the nail plate and do not desquamate.\")\n34400:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30904566\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4052034 \"A thymic tuft cell is a subset of terminally differentiated medullary thymic epithelial cell comprising 5-10% of total mTECs. Lineage-tracing studies indicate that this cell arises from mature MHCII mTECs, with development occurring through both Aire-dependent and Aire-independent pathways. However, its exact origins remain unclear.\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
